 - **Fix:** collect per-pass write facts independently of the lookahead switch and omit only stores of attachments that were loaded and provably unchanged. Clears, depth writes, stencil writes and possible writable image/atomic/storage aliases retain their stores. Lookahead, pass merging and cross-submission invalidation remain disabled. `DM_NVN_UNWRITTEN_DC=0` restores store-all behavior.
 - **Check:** `make -C dm/gfx/tests GAME=<id> check_t_unwritten_store` performs real GPU readback against a store-all control and literal color/depth/stencil values, with lookahead disabled. It covers read-only depth/stencil, depth writes, stencil writes, pending clears, and writable images (including native image atomics) and both storage-buffer binding forms. `t_unwritten_store --bench` runs a synthetic 32-pass 1080p workload with balanced on/off order; it is not a game FPS measurement.
 - **Found on:** [NieR:Automata US 1.0.3](../../dm/games/010056B015FE8000/README.md#factory-combat-capture-and-9s-texture-follow-up), during iPhone factory-combat performance investigation. The change passes the GPU proof and rendering regressions on Mac; iPhone gameplay benefit remains to be measured.
+
+### Render-pass reuse and compression without removing feedback copies
+
+- **Symptom:** repeated identical render targets end render passes; ordinary feedback snapshots request arbitrary pixel-format views.
+- **Cause:** exact-target continuation was coupled to speculative lookahead; unconditional PixelFormatView usage disables lossless compression on supported Apple GPUs.
+- **Fix:** continue identical full-attachment passes only while resource generations and CPU-write epochs match; preserve clear, shader-write and attachment-read boundaries. Ordinary color writes require both enabled channels and a real shader output. Request format-view usage only for actual reinterpretation, upgrading from the retained snapshot rather than a newer attachment. `DM_NVN_PASS_REUSE=0` restores the prior policy. Diagnostic counters are atomic across encoding and presentation.
+- **Check:** the backport includes the upstream feedback readback, exact-target, registry-change and unwritten-store regressions. Build and device results are recorded separately; source integration is not a sustained-FPS result.
+- **Found on:** [Breath of the Wild](../../dm/games/01007EF00011E000/README.md#render-pass-backport-2026-11-01), following the reported M3 iPad frame drop.
